   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "EDITING & STRUCTURE\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 33 to 48\n   1 Number of main characters\n   2 Groups in the hour\n   3 Exit\n   4 How often a main is in the season\n   5 Scene change rate\n   6 Sequence lengths\n   7 How a scene begins\n   8 How scenes join (storytelling)\n   9 Call and response\n  10 Repetition scheme\n  11 Signature image or line\n  12 Contrast map\n  13 Tension\n  14 Energy\n  15 Visual density\n  16 Constant\nCV-CC 2: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 49 to 64\n   1 Psych-out shift\n   2 Clipped or flowing cuts\n   3 Human touch in camera and cuts\n   4 Motif shape\n   5 Cross-cutting\n   6 When the audience learns it\n   7 Story point of view\n   8 Scene length\n   9 How the scene ends\n  10 The opening grab\n  11 Ends where it starts\n  12 Multicam angle switching\n  13 Nested scene\n  14 Time and speed\n  15 Shots in order\n  16 suite: Two-person hour\nCV-CC 3: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 65 to 80\n   1 suite: Build\n   2 suite: Drop\n   3 suite: Signature return\n   4 suite: Crime, Tarantino style\n   5 suite: Horror\n   6 suite: Action\n   7 suite: Western\n   8 suite: Musical\n   9 suite: Documentary look (camera and light)\n  10 suite: Surrealist\n  11 suite: Romantic comedy\n  12 suite: Viral short: hook and loop\n  13 suite: Episode cliffhanger\n  14 suite: Stop-motion feel\n  15 suite: The big moment\n  16 suite: Breakneck pace\nCV-CC 4: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 81 to 96\n   1 suite: Slow and patient\n   2 suite: Cut like music\n   3 suite: Ensemble patchwork\n   4 suite: Losing a main character\n   5 suite: Studio sitcom\n   6 suite: A story inside the story\n   7 suite: Long talk that snaps into violence\n   8 pair: When tension peaks, a long silence\n   9 pair: When energy drops, the hold is long\n  10 pair: When suite Build, suite Drop\n  11 pair: When suite Aggressive camera, suite Quiet confession\n  12 pair: When suite Storm, suite Breathing room\n  13 pair: When time slows, the bits in the air hang\n  14 pair: When scenes start changing faster, the tension climbs\n  15 pair: When tension climbs, scenes get shorter\n  16 pair: When the hour splits into two groups, the film cuts back and forth between them\nCV-CC 5: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 2, CC 97 to 112\n   1 pair: When the film cuts between two places faster and faster, the clock feels tighter\n   2 pair: When a scene starts in the middle of the action, the audience starts asking questions\n   3 pair: When every shot answers the one before, laughs come faster\n   4 pair: When shots come in threes, the third one becomes the punchline\n   5 pair: When the same moment keeps repeating, it turns into a running gag\n   6 pair: When the film's signature image comes back, the old feeling comes back with it\n   7 pair: When scenes are built to clash, the feeling flips at the cut\n   8 pair: When one sound or image is held under everything, dread builds\n   9 pair: When a scare turns out to be fake, the audience laughs with relief\n  10 pair: When the cuts get louder and sharper, the energy jumps\n  11 pair: When the camera feels like a nosy person in the room, awkward moments get more awkward\n  12 pair: When a repeating tune or image keeps climbing, hope climbs with it\n  13 pair: When the story hops between characters, the audience learns things before they do\n  14 pair: When a main character shows up more often, their own story gets heavier\n  15 pair: When more main characters share the spotlight, their stories start crossing\n  16 pair: When a main character dies, the tears come soon after\nCV-CC 6: PORT 2 (your second cable), MIDI channel 3, CC 1 to 9\n   1 pair: When a scene plays out inside another scene, the audience starts doubting what's real\n   2 pair: When the shots get short, the energy climbs\n   3 pair: When the talk runs long and casual, violence arrives without warning\n   4 pair: When a chapter card appears, the story jumps to someone else's side\n   5 pair: When a false scare passes, the real one comes right after\n   6 pair: When the cutting jumps between the crew, the tension climbs\n   7 pairs: Long-form shape\n   8 pairs: The squeeze\n   9 pairs: Long talk that snaps into violence: the moves"
   },
